<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gugong Danfu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ancient Duke Danfu, King Tai of Zhou</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gugong Danfu, 'the Ancient Duke Danfu', was a legendary ancestor of the Zhou royal house and the grandfather of King Wen. According to tradition he led the Zhou people from Bin to the plain of Zhouyuan below <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-qi">Mount Qi</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> to escape attacks by nomadic peoples, laying the foundation of the later Zhou state. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/later-zhou">Later Zhou</a> kings honoured him with the posthumous title King Tai.</p></div>
